 robots joining together, with the process of that unification varying over time. Produced by Peter Keefe (executive producer) and Ted Koplar through his production company World Events Productions, Voltron was an adaptation of several Japanese anime television series from Toei Company. The original television series aired in syndication from September 10, 1984, to November 18, 1985. The first season of Voltron, featuring the \"Lion Force Voltron\", was adapted from the series Beast King GoLion. The second season, featuring the \"Vehicle Team Voltron\", was adapted from the unrelated series Armored Fleet Dairugger XV.\n\nVoltron: Defender of the Universe was the top-rated syndicated children's show for two years during its original run, and it spawned three follow-up series, several comic books, and a line of toys.","evidence":"documented","universe":"voltron-toys","aliases":["Voltron"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[{"id":"66265ea5-5443-49aa-93a7-df5839a64503","relationship":"connected_to","title":"Takashi Shirogane and Voltron appear together in mapped lore.","explanation":"Takashi Shirogane's entry mentions Voltron — Voltron is an American animated television series franchise that features a team of space explorers who pilot a giant super robot known as \"Voltron\".","strength":"0.7200","discovery_score":"0.7800","direction":"incoming","from_entity_id":"6aa7b789-be96-41e4-aad9-ecf24d641b01","to_entity_id":"101a7b92-2e25-4d24-9446-90449e5ddb03","entity_id":"6aa7b789-be96-41e4-aad9-ecf24d641b01","slug":"takashi-shirogane","name":"Takashi Shirogane","type":"person","short_description":"Takashi Shirogane (銀 貴, Shirogane Takashi), known as Sven Holgersson in the original English dub of Beast King GoLion as Voltron, as well as in an alternate universe in Voltron: Legendary Defender, is a fictional…","evidence":"fiction","image_url":null,"path":"/voltron-toys/takashi-shirogane","kind":"character","type_label":"Character"}],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"voltron-toys","title":"Voltron is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Voltron, related names, marks, and materials are the property of World Events / DreamWorks / respective rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent educational encyclopedia project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification marks, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"voltron-toys","name":"Voltron","theme":"voltron-toys","path":"/voltron-toys","logo":null,"categories":["toys"]}}